,"label":"Rushing Touchdowns","value":"0"},{"name":"yardsPerRushAttempt","label":"YDS/RA","value":"4.2"}],"birthPlace":"Antioch, CA","draftText":"2024: Rd 4, Pk 132 (DET)"},"news":[{"headline":"Bills QB Josh Allen struggles vs. Chiefs in 'grossest' conditions","description":"The Bills won their 10th game of the season on Thursday vs. the Chiefs, but QB Josh Allen struggled in the weather, passing for only 81 yards.","published":"2026-11-27T07:09:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609813/bills-qb-josh-allen-struggles-vs-chiefs-grossest-conditions","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nick Suss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Eagles QB Joe Milton wows teammates with breakout game in Dallas","description":"Eagles QB Joe Milton had a breakout game on the national stage, accounting for four touchdowns in a wild 39-38 come-from-behind win over the Cowboys.","published":"2026-11-27T06:10:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609081/eagles-qb-joe-milton-wows-teammates-breakout-game-dallas","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bills edge Chiefs with last-second FG in low-scoring battle","description":"The Bills won their seventh straight, snapping the Chiefs' win streak at three in a sloppy, low-scoring thriller.","published":"2026-11-27T05:59:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50582828/2026-nfl-buffalo-bills-kansas-city-chiefs-thanksgiving","type":"Story","byline":"Nick Suss and Nate Taylor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Jerry Jones backs Schottenheimer despite 'damning setbacks' in loss","description":"Jerry Jones said he did not anticipate making immediate changes but still labeled the Cowboys' latest fourth-quarter collapse as a \"damning\" setback.","published":"2026-11-27T05:17:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50608969/cowboys-jerry-jones-backs-coach-damning-setbacks","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Todd Archer","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Will Shipley brushes off argument with coach Nick Sirianni: 'Emotions were running high'","description":"RB Will Shipley likened his sideline argument with coach Nick Sirianni to a Thanksgiving family spat in the wake of the Eagles' dramatic comeback win at Dallas.","published":"2026-11-27T06:26:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50608884/will-shipley-brushes-argument-coach-nick-sirianni","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tomlin upset by Rodgers' bitter exit, calls situation 'a dumpster fire'","description":"Mike Tomlin said he was saddened by Aaron Rodgers' tumultuous exit from Pittsburgh and disagreed with how the QB \"aired out\" his grievances against Mike McCarthy.","published":"2026-11-27T05:02:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50608802/tomlin-calls-rodgers-mccarthy-situation-dumpster-fire","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Brooke Pryor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"QB Caleb Williams, WR Rome Odunze's chemistry helps Bears stun Lions","description":"QB Caleb Williams and WR Rome Odunze leaned on their chemistry and trust to secure Chicago's ninth win of the season.","published":"2026-11-27T03:58:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50608495/qb-caleb-williams-wr-rome-odunze-chemistry-helps-bears-stun-lions","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Courtney Cronin","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Eagles' comeback against Cowboys stuns Jason Kelce, Caitlin Clark and more","description":"The Philadelphia Eagles pulled off the largest Thanksgiving Day comeback in NFL history.","published":"2026-11-27T02:36:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50607960/eagles-cowboys-thanksgiving-social-reaction","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Joe Milton has huge game as Eagles shock Cowboys","description":"Dallas blew a 21-point lead as Philly made a spectacular comeback with Milton at the helm.","published":"2026-11-27T02:43:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50605786/cowboys-eagles-thanksgiving-dak-prescott-saquon-barkley","type":"Story","byline":"Todd Archer and Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Brady disappointed in Rodgers' McCarthy comments: 'Nobody wins'","description":"Tom Brady expressed his disappointment in how Aaron Rodgers handled his exit from Pittsburgh, saying there are things in the locker room that shouldn't be made public.","published":"2026-11-27T03:07:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50607635/tom-brady-disappointed-aaron-rodgers-mccarthy-comments","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Sione Vaki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sione_Vaki","description":"American football player (born 2001)","touched":"2026-11-26T23:15:21Z","intro":"Sione Vaki (born July 30, 2001) is an American professional football running back for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Utah Utes as a two-way player. Vaki was selected by the Lions in the fourth round of the 2024 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Vaki attended Liberty High School in Brentwood, California. In high school, he played on both sides of the ball. On offense he rushed for 401 yards and seven touchdowns, while also bringing in 107 receptions for 2,203 yards and 32 touchdowns. On defense, he notched 142 tackles with one being for a loss, five interceptions, four fumble recoveries, two forced fumbles, and two defensive touchdowns, Vaki also returned a kickoff for a touchdown. Vaki committed to play college football at the University of Utah."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his true freshman season, Vaki totalled 41 tackles with 3.5 going for a loss, three pass deflections, and a forced fumble in the 2022 season.\nIn week one of the 2023 season, he recorded his first career interception versus the Florida Gators. In week seven, Vaki had a breakout game where he played both ways of the ball as he rushed 15 times for 158 yards and two touchdown to help the Utes beat California. In the following week, he rushed nine times for 68 yards, while also hauling in five receptions for 149 yards and two touchdowns, while also notching two tackles and having the best coverage grade on the Utes, as helped them upset USC 34–32.  The rest of the season, the Utes formulated a plan to use Vaki more on offense.\nAs a sophomore, Vaki finished the season with 51 tackles, 8.5 tackles for a loss, two sacks and two interceptions on defense. On offense he had 317 yards rushing (7.5 yards per carry) and two rushing touchdowns. As well as 11 receptions for 203 yards and three receiving touchdowns. He was voted to the first-team All-Pac-12 team twice in 2023, both as a safety and a special teams/all-purpose player. Following the 2023 season, Vaki declared for the 2024 NFL draft after playing two seasons of college football, as he went on a three-year mission trip following his high school graduation."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"Vaki was selected in the fourth round, 132nd overall, by the Detroit Lions in the 2024 NFL draft. He was named to the PFWA All-Rookie Team."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Vaki lost his mother Oto’ota due to cancer.  Vaki is a member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints; he started to serve a mission for the church in the Nuku'alofa, Tonga, Mission, but was reassigned to the West Salt Lake City, Utah, Mission due to the COVID-19 pandemic."}],"wikidataId":"Q123321999","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4912274","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/V/VakiSi00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/sione-vaki/158505","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/sione-vaki/11740","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sione_Vaki"},"insights":["On the field for 21% of Detroit’s offensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.2M is the 33rd-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2027.","Drafted 132nd overall in 2024 (round 4) by DET."]}